      "title": "Rank Group posts record £834.1m FY26 revenue and 21% profit growth despite 40% UK remote gaming duty",
      "text": "Rank Group's preliminary results for the 12 months to 30 June 2026, published on 13 August, show like-for-like net gaming revenue up 6% to £834.1m - a fifth consecutive year of growth across every business unit. Underlying operating profit rose 21% to £78.6m, the operating margin improved to 9.4%, return on capital employed strengthened to 18.3% and the total dividend was raised 35%. Digital revenue advanced 8% for the year with like-for-like growth accelerating to 12% in Q4, achieved while Rank cut above-the-line marketing spend specifically to absorb the increase in UK Remote Gaming Duty to 40%. Statutory profit was weaker than underlying, reflecting separately disclosed items including a payment fraud incident in Spain and costs tied to a UK regulatory settlement; Rank's 14 July trading update had flagged a proposed £5m payment in lieu of a financial penalty covering historical compliance failings at Grosvenor Casinos between 1 November 2024 and 1 May 2025, which the Gambling Commission was 'minded to accept'. The group secured a new four-year £120m revolving credit facility, ended the year with net cash of £56.8m pre-IFRS 16 against reported net debt of £147.2m, and reiterated a medium-term ambition of at least £100m underlying operating profit. Management warned that further tax increases on bingo halls and casinos could make some venues economically unviable.",
