    "expanded": "The regulator said conditions in affected zones can hinder the online, real-time operation of localised games, novelty games and internet-operated games, and can affect timely compliance with obligations for information transmission and for the settlement and payment of exploitation rights and administration expenses. It will prioritise evaluating transitional measures specifically in information transmission, reporting deadlines, and settlement and payment of those levies, citing the principles of efficacy, celerity, economy, coordination and good faith under Article 209 of Colombia's Constitution and its competences under Decree 4142 of 2011, Decree 1451 of 2015 and Law 643 of 2001. Coljuegos was explicit about the limits: any measure will be strictly transitional and will not entail debt forgiveness or waiver of collection, describing the aim as a reasonable and proportional adjustment of obligations given exceptional circumstances. It also emphasised it will guarantee the exclusive allocation of monopoly revenues to health services under Article 336 of the Constitution, and will keep service channels open for operator reports, queries and requests, with information from sector trade associations incorporated into the analysis. No resolution number, decision deadline or count of affected operators has been given.",
